---
<EditorialShell 
  title="Productivity Caller | Kotlin Reminder App | Shivam Mahajan" 
  description="See how Shivam Mahajan built Productivity Caller with Kotlin and Jetpack Compose, using phone calls for reminders and natural language parsing." 
  eyebrow="Move 001 / Kotlin" 
  heading="Productivity Caller" 
  intro="A native Kotlin and Jetpack Compose reminder app that uses phone calls instead of push notifications. Covers reminder architecture, natural language parser, and platform constraints."
  structuredData={structuredData}
>
  <a slot="actions" href="https://drive.google.com/file/d/1O9mQD-Qeo7GR40SdG440pdqSM8NdXV_K/view?usp=sharing" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Watch Demo ↗</a>
  <a slot="actions" href="/resume/">View Resume</a>

  <!-- Top-of-page Breadcrumbs (Tactic #88 & Tactic #98) -->
  <nav class="breadcrumb-nav" aria-label="Breadcrumb navigation">
    <a href="/">Home</a> <span>/</span>
    <a href="/projects/">Projects</a> <span>/</span>
    <a href="https://shivammahajan.com/projects/productivity-caller/" aria-current="page">Productivity Caller</a>
  </nav>

  <!-- Author Byline linked to profile (Tactic #60) -->
  <div class="byline-bar">
    <span>By <a href="/resume/">Shivam Mahajan</a> (Software Developer)</span>
    <span>·</span>
    <time datetime="2026-10-10">October 2026</time>
    <span>·</span>
    <span>Android Architecture Case Study</span>
  </div>

  <!-- Direct Answer Executive Summary (Tactic #2) -->
  <div class="direct-answer">
    <p><strong>Executive Summary:</strong> Productivity Caller is a native Android application built in Kotlin and Jetpack Compose that solves notification blindness by replacing ignorable push notifications with automated incoming phone calls. It features a custom regex-based natural language parser supporting 80+ datetime permutations.</p>
  </div>

  <!-- Hard Quantitative Statistics (Tactic #3 & Tactic #69) -->
  <div class="metrics-strip">
    <div class="metric-pill">
      <span class="metric-label">Parser Patterns</span>
      <span class="metric-value">80+ Formats</span>
    </div>
    <div class="metric-pill">
      <span class="metric-label">UI Architecture</span>
      <span class="metric-value">Jetpack Compose</span>
    </div>
    <div class="metric-pill">
      <span class="metric-label">Language</span>
      <span class="metric-value">100% Kotlin</span>
    </div>
    <div class="metric-pill">
      <span class="metric-label">Notification Type</span>
      <span class="metric-value">Direct Calls</span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section><h2>What it does</h2><p>Instead of a standard push notification, a scheduled reminder utilizes a direct phone call interface. The demo shows the app's user flow, ensuring high-priority tasks successfully grab the user's immediate attention.</p></section>
  <section><h2>My contribution</h2><p>Shivam architected and built the entire Android application utilizing Kotlin and Jetpack Compose for the modern declarative UI. He also engineered a pattern-based parser for entering tasks accurately using natural language.</p></section>
  <section><h2>Parsing reminders</h2><p>The custom natural-language parser algorithm successfully recognizes more than 80 distinct input patterns and date-time permutations, according to the project resume. Its exact coverage and automated evaluation methods ensure users can quickly type complex recurring schedules.</p></section>
  <section><h2>Calls and platform constraints</h2><p>Phone calls are central to the reminder experience. Handling strict Android device permissions, varied operating-system behavior, background execution limits, and delivery reliability required deep integration with Android's Telephony and AlarmManager APIs.</p></section>
  <section><h2>Testing and limitations</h2><p>The project resume reports extensive unit testing to validate the parsing engine logic. Robust test suites verify the date manipulations and lifecycle states, providing confidence in the production release candidate.</p></section>
</EditorialShell>

